{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>Placed upon her shoulder.</b> The <b>waterskin</b>, as a sign of servitude, after the manner of וְהִתְעַנִּי תַּחַת יָדֶיהָ (Genesis 16:9). Yet the righteous man did not cease to give them sufficient for their needs, as the Sages, of blessed memory, stated: וַיְהִי אֱלֹהִים אֶת הַנַּעַר (Genesis 21:20) serves to include his donkeys, camels, and servants. Therefore they lacked nothing but water while they wandered in the wilderness; and once water was found, he dwelt there in the wilderness according to his nature, for he was a פֶּרֶא אָדָם (a wild man)." "<b>And the child.</b> He gave her the child as well." "<b>And he sent her away.</b> He escorted her with abundant kindness, as in וְאַבְרָהָם הֹלֵךְ עִמָּם לְשַׁלְּחָם (Genesis 18:16)."], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:31:01.762713453Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}